// The CONSOLE end of a remote-REPL relay, over UDP so it runs on one laptop.
//
//   ./csp -i examples/relay/node.csp          (one window -- the node)
//   ./csp -i examples/relay/master.csp        (the other -- type here)
//
// Ctrl-] hands the keyboard to the far end, Ctrl-] again takes it back. The
// prompt says [remote] and [local].
//
// FOUR BUFFERS, not two: `in` and `out` on one buffer share ONE heap block, so
// a buffer cannot be both the key source and the screen sink -- the display
// bytes land on top of the keys and get sent back out as input. That is not
// theoretical; it is what the first version of this file did, and the far end
// received `sys.sys.Id =Id = 42`.
//
// FOUR BYTES per cycle each way: a whole-buffer assignment carries 32 bits, so
// the buffers are 4 and the relay moves one word per cycle. Enough to type at;
// a listing crawls. See TODO.md for why raising it wants a route rather than a
// rule.

#buffer Keys:4 in  console             // what was typed here
#buffer Show:4 out console             // what to put on this screen
#buffer Tx:4   out udp 55801 127.0.0.1 // to the node
#buffer Rx:4   in  udp 55800           // from the node

// Keys out. .dlc first: it says how many of the four bytes are real, and the
// datagram carries exactly that many -- padding would arrive as NULs in the far
// end's line editor.
Tx.dlc = Keys.dlc ? Keys.rx
Tx = Keys         ? Keys.rx
Tx.tx = 1         ? Keys.rx

// And what the node printed, onto this screen.
Show.dlc = Rx.dlc ? Rx.rx
Show = Rx         ? Rx.rx
Show.tx = 1       ? Rx.rx
